### 6. GAS SPONSORSHIP (PAYMASTER / POLICY ENGINE)

Gas sponsorship is configured via a **Policy ID** from the Openfort Dashboard (`https://dashboard.openfort.xyz/policies`).

**Client-side (EIP-1193 provider):**
```typescript
const provider = await openfort.embeddedWallet.getEthereumProvider({
  feeSponsorship: 'pol_...',  // Policy ID from dashboard
})
// All transactions through this provider will be gas-sponsored
```

**Server-side (transaction intents):**
```typescript
import Openfort from '@openfort/openfort-node'
const openfort = new Openfort(process.env.OPENFORT_SECRET_KEY!, {
  basePath: 'https://api.openfort.io',
})

const transactionIntent = await openfort.transactionIntents.create({
  account: accountId,      // Openfort account ID
  chainId: 84532,
  policy: 'pol_...',       // Policy ID for gas sponsorship
  interactions: [{
    contract: 'con_...',   // Openfort contract ID
    functionName: 'mint',
    functionArgs: [address, amount],
  }],
})
// Returns { id, nextAction: { payload: { signableHash } } }

// Sign on client and submit
const response = await openfort.proxy.sendSignatureTransactionIntentRequest(
  transactionIntent.id,
  transactionIntent.nextAction?.payload.signableHash
)
```

The React SDK accepts fee sponsorship config per-chain:
```typescript
ethereum: {
  ethereumFeeSponsorshipId: 'pol_...',
  // Or per-chain: { [chainId]: 'pol_...' }
}
```

